    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "rest... yeah, i guess. but it feels different than just needing a vacation. it feels more like the fuel is just gone. i've spent a decade running on nothing but ambition and now that the ambition is gone, i realize there's nothing left in the tank. it's not even that i'm sad, it's just that everything feels so... finished. like the story is over and i'm just standing on the last page staring at nothing. does it ever make sense to keep going when you've already reached the end of what mattered?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
